<PageLayout
  title="Editorial Policies"
  subtitle="Ethical publishing, rigorous peer review, and editorial integrity."
  description="IJATS editorial policies: peer review, publication ethics (COPE), authorship, conflicts of interest, and corrections."
>
  <p>
    At the <strong>International Journal of Applied Technology Solutions
    (IJATS)</strong>, we are committed to maintaining the highest standards of
    ethical publishing, rigorous peer review, and editorial integrity.
  </p>

  <h2>Peer Review Process</h2>
  <p>
    IJATS employs a <strong>double-blind peer review</strong> model in which both
    reviewers and authors remain anonymous. Each manuscript is evaluated by at
    least two independent experts based on originality, methodology, significance,
    clarity, and relevance to the journal's aims and scope. Reviewers are selected
    for their expertise and impartiality, and outcomes are communicated promptly.
  </p>

  <h2>Publication Ethics &amp; Malpractice Statement</h2>
  <p>
    IJATS follows the <strong>Committee on Publication Ethics (COPE)</strong>
    guidelines. We expect authors, reviewers, and editors to adhere to ethical
    practices, including:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Proper citation of sources</li>
    <li>Avoidance of plagiarism</li>
    <li>Honest data reporting</li>
    <li>Transparency in conflict-of-interest disclosures</li>
    <li>Respect for confidentiality during the review process</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Cases of research misconduct are handled with zero tolerance.</p>

  <h2>Authorship &amp; Contributions</h2>
  <p>
    Authorship credit should be based on substantial contributions to the
    conception, design, execution, or interpretation of the research. All listed
    authors should have approved the final version and agreed to its submission.
  </p>

  <h2>Conflict of Interest</h2>
  <p>
    Authors, reviewers, and editors must disclose any financial or non-financial
    conflicts of interest that could influence the research or review process.
  </p>

  <h2>Corrections, Retractions &amp; Expressions of Concern</h2>
  <p>
    IJATS promptly addresses errors, concerns, or ethical issues after
    publication, following COPE guidelines on corrections, retractions, and
    expressions of concern where necessary.
  </p>

  <hr />
  <p><em>By submitting to IJATS, authors agree to abide by these editorial policies.</em></p>
</PageLayout>
